+# GHDL cross-format fixtures
+
+These are three configurations of the adjacent VHDL design. All timescales are
+1 fs. GHDL writes GHW and VCD in the same invocation. GTKWave vcd2fst converts
+that VCD to the plain `.fst` file. A separate GHDL run with identical inputs
+and `--fst` produces `.native.fst`. GHW and native FST both capture the record.
+VCD and the FST derived from it only capture the scalar marker.
+
+| Run | Marker rises | packet.flag |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| baseline | 10 ns | stays low |
+| delayed | 11 ns | stays low |
+| record_change | 10 ns | high from 10 to 20 ns |
+
+The marker falls at 20 ns. packet.valid rises at 10 ns and falls at 20 ns in
+all three runs. From this directory, regenerate with
+`python3 generate.py --output .` (GHDL with VHDL-2008 support and vcd2fst on
+PATH). Timestamp headers may change. The Rust tests use the checked-in fixtures
+and do not need either generator.
